      "lines": "54-59",
      "evidence": "The actual shutdown_and_drain future is pinned and manually polled. The oneshot barrier is sent only after that poll returns Pending. Before aborting the test caller, assertions require it still unfinished, the actual coordinator JoinSlot ticket mutex held and the real connection unjoined. Later full drain still requires all actual coordinator/connection/producer joins. No production ticket or worker is aborted."
    },
    {
      "id": "TRANSPORT-02",
      "resolution": "CLOSED_IN_SOURCE_NOT_EXECUTED",
      "path": "crates/app/src/server/transport_tests.rs",
      "lines": "39-44,87-100,122-125",
      "evidence": "The response producer sends only its first64KiB then blocks on an explicit release channel; actual unfinished/joined0 state is checked before and at T0. The verified original spool still completes verification before headers, then a fixture-only Body adapter permits one actual source chunk and blocks before another, with waiting=true, release=false, joined0 and one charged spool lease at T0. Its unchanged2MiB tail exceeds the unchanged four-chunk spool queue. Both controlled responses are released after T0 and retain exact bytes/hash/tail/normalEOF/noabort/cleanup assertions. All negative fixtures use the None/no-wrapper path."
    },
    {
      "id": "TRANSPORT-03",
      "resolution": "CLOSED_IN_SOURCE_NOT_EXECUTED",
      "path": "crates/app/src/server/transport_tests.rs",
      "lines": "156-166",
      "evidence": "A real accepted TcpStream is owned by IncomingIo. An actual response producer control is bound inside retained request scope and remains active, alongside a live ordering-probe lease. No global abort/quiesce/cancel_all runs before the oracle. Only drop(io) sets io_dropped and invokes active callbacks; the probe checks that ordering, the peer observes actual TCP EOF, and pending.ready must fail from cancellation before any shutdown/drain can mask it. Actual worker and response supervisor joins, retained0/complete0 and binding pruning are then asserted. Immediate detection of unpolled remote FIN is not claimed."
    }
